**Summary of fixes:**

| Previous error | Fix |
|---|---|
| `fflib_DataAccess` type / `DATA_ACCESS_USER_MODE` constant don't exist | fflib's `setDataAccess` accepts a **String**. Use `this.setDataAccess('USER_MODE')`. |
| `Schema.DescribeSObjectResult.getFieldSets()` doesn't exist | Apex has no runtime field-set enumeration API. List the field-set fields (`AnnualRevenue`, `Rating`) explicitly with a comment to keep them in sync. |
| `getDataAccess().dataAccessScope` doesn't exist | `getDataAccess()` returns a `String`; compare against `'SYSTEM_MODE'` / `'USER_MODE'`. |
| `DescribeFieldResult.getNamespace()` doesn't exist | Removed. Only standard objects are used, so `getDescribe().getName()` gives the full API name. |

Looking at the error, `fflib_IDomains` is not a valid type in this deployed version. Since `fflib_ISObjectSelector` works as a top-level interface (proven by `ICasesSelector.cls` compiling), the unit of work interface follows the same pattern: `fflib_IUnitOfWork`.

