**What changed and why**

| Prior error | Fix |
|---|---|
| `fflib_SObjectDomain(String)` – constructor not defined | The deployed `fflib_SObjectDomain` constructor accepts an **`SObjectType`**, not a `String`. Use `SObjectType.getGlobalDescribe().get('Account')` / `get('Contact')`. |
| `fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork()` no-arg constructor not defined | Pass the explicit `List<fflib_ISObjectDomain>` to the UOW constructor so it knows which object domains to manage. |
| `addSObject(Account)` / `addSObjects(List<SObject>)` – "method does not exist" | These errors were **cascades** from the constructor failures (once the UOW variable's type is unresolvable, every call on it reports "method not found"). With the constructor fixed, the standard `addSObject(SObject)` resolves correctly because both `Account` and `Contact` implement `SObject`. |
| Bulk-safety | `addSObject` merely queues the record in memory; `commitWork()` issues **one** `INSERT` per SObject type. Calling it in a loop over hundreds of contacts is well within governor limits. |

